BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancasterpa": "https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/lancaster-breakfast-and-history-walking-tour/2026-08-22/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancasterpa
X-SOURCE:Discover Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T110000
DTSTAMP:20251008T153805Z
CREATED:20250708T130742Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251008T153805Z
UID:10044839-1787389200-1787396400@lancasterpa.com
SUMMARY:Lancaster Breakfast and History Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Searching for a walking history tour in Lancaster? You’re in for a flavorful experience—literally! \n\n\nIntroducing the Lancaster History & Breakfast Walking Tour—a dynamic two-hour adventure that blends the rich heritage of one of America’s oldest inland cities with a delicious morning meal. Explore Lancaster’s vibrant streets with a professionally trained local guide and journey through time from the early 1700s through the transformative decades of the 20th century. \n\n\nBrought to you by Unique Lancaster Experiences\, this guided walk kicks off with your choice of hot or iced coffee or tea to energize your morning. Along the way\, you’ll hear engaging stories about Lancaster’s evolution as a bustling Market City and its transition from trolleys to automobiles after WWI. \n\n\nBut this isn’t your standard history tour. You’ll dive into interactive discussions and uncover captivating insights about colonial life\, architectural landmarks\, and the impact of prohibition on the region. \n\n\nAs you explore\, you’ll stop at five handpicked local spots to enjoy a curated tasting menu featuring hearty breakfast sandwiches\, fresh fruits\, sweet pastries\, and other morning favorites. \n\n\nPlease note: This tour offers vegetarian-friendly options only. If you have other dietary needs\, we recommend our International Food Tour for a better fit. \n\n\nWhether you’re passionate about history\, love discovering new flavors\, or just want a memorable way to see the city\, the Lancaster History & Breakfast Tour is a great choice for solo explorers\, couples\, and groups alike.
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/lancaster-breakfast-and-history-walking-tour/2026-08-22/
LOCATION:Unique Lancaster\, 23 N Walnut Street\, Lancaster\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Children & Family Events,Food & Beverage Events,Lancaster City,Tour
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lancasterpa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/unique-lancaster-experiences-event-breakfast-tour.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancasterpa": "https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/bastidas-soccer-academy-training-camp/2026-08-22/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancasterpa
X-SOURCE:Discover Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T130000
DTSTAMP:20260401T171137Z
CREATED:20260401T171137Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260401T171137Z
UID:10048190-1787389200-1787403600@lancasterpa.com
SUMMARY:Bastidas Soccer Academy Training Camp
DESCRIPTION:Established in 1999\, the Bastidas Soccer Academy emphasizes the importance of basic skill and ball mastery.  We are passionate about teaching you to have fun and develop a winning attitude. \nAll boys and girls from any school or district\, entering grades 3-8\, are invited to attend this premier camp to kick off the fall season. Registration is $200 per player (or $190 each for a sibling group) and will include: \n\nCamp T-shirt\nUSSF Licensed Coaches (including “A” License coach Trajano Bastidas) and USYS ODP Coaches\nCamp features– league play\, king of the hill\, soccer dance\, small sided games\, stations\nMain focuses– first touch\, passing\, receiving\, finishing\, having fun!\n\nPlayers should arrive at least 10 minutes early each day with proper attire\, sneakers\, cleats\, shin guards\, plenty of water\, and a snack for the mid-point break. \nQuestions? Please reach out to bastidasa@manheimcentral.org \nSee you at Camp! \n* You will see “Zeffy” on your credit card statement \n** The optional platform donation at checkout can be set to any amount\, or $0
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/bastidas-soccer-academy-training-camp/2026-08-22/
LOCATION:Manheim Central Middle School\, 261 White Oak Rd\, Manheim\, 17545\, United States
CATEGORIES:Children & Family Events,Manheim,Outdoor Activities,Sports,Summer Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lancasterpa.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Bastidas-Soccer-Camp.png
END:VEVENT
