BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Fig Lancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/w-miller-barbour-his-prospect-for-freedom/", "Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/w-miller-barbour-his-prospect-freedom-189387"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/w-miller-barbour-his-prospect-for-freedom/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster, Lancaster Libraries
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T190000
DTSTAMP:20260714T161548Z
CREATED:20260710T142835Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260714T161548Z
UID:10014787-1789063200-1789066800@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:W. Miller Barbour & His Prospect For Freedom
DESCRIPTION:Join public historian Eric Schubert for a talk about a pioneering Pennsylvania human rights leader whose activism helped define mid-20th-century civil rights goals. This independent presentation explores Barbour’s remarkable journey from central Pennsylvania to the forefront of early civil rights activism and examines the enduring legacy of a forgotten champion for equality.Long before the modern Civil Rights Movement\, W. Miller Barbour (1908–1957) dedicated his life to advancing racial equality and human rights. A Middletown native and Elizabethtown College graduate\, Barbour rose from local roots to become a pioneering civil rights leader\, serving with the Urban League in Denver and Los Angeles. Through advocacy\, community organizing\, and interracial dialogue\, he expanded opportunities for African Americans decades before the landmark victories of the 1960s. \n\n\n\n Eric Schubert is a public historian\, genealogist\, and forensic genetic genealogist as seen on Good Morning America and more. He serves on the Executive Committee of the Historic Preservation Trust of Lancaster County and is a White House Historical Association Next-Gen Leader. Schubert earned his M.A. in History at Millersville University. He was part of the research team which contributed to the award-winning documentary The Prospect for Freedom: W. Miller Barbour’s Human Rights Journey and independently organized the W. Miller Barbour Lecture Series alongside Abigail Sholes\, which seeks to reintroduce Barbour’s legacy to communities across Pennsylvania.
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/w-miller-barbour-his-prospect-for-freedom/
LOCATION:Lancsater Public Library\, 151 N. Queen Street\, Lancaster\, 17603
CATEGORIES:Community
ORGANIZER;CN="Lancaster Public Library":MAILTO:lkaliss@lancasterpubliclibrary.org
END:VEVENT
