UID:ab42c4fd686f8260dd50ce147b99ae4c@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, STEM\, Everyone\n\nCider Making with Park Naturali
 st Lisa Sanchez of Lancaster County Parks and Rec.A program for the whole 
 family where you will explore the history of the apple tree and make fresh
  cider with an old fashioned cider press. Apples will be provided for the 
 cider making. Participants will help make and drink the cider. Program is 
 scheduled to be held outdoor\, please dress for the weather. Registration 
 is required. Please register each family member individually to help us ke
 ep an accurate headcount. Ages 2 and younger do NOT require registration. 
 Thank you! A liability waiver MUST be signed by each participant. (please 
 see document to the right)This program take place in the field at the Envi
 ronmental Education Center at Lancaster County Parks. Address: One Nature'
 s Way\, Lancaster\, PA 17602.
LOCATION:Columbia
