X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/dramatic-play-friday-169343"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Dramatic Play Friday
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T154500
UID:6ab3fa07c3a3f0c6715ffa58f3ea814f@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Toddlers\, Children\n\nDrop-in program. No registration requir
 ed.Join us for a fun-filled adventure at the library! Children ages 2–7 
 are invited to explore their creativity and imagination through hands-on p
 retend play. This free program offers three exciting stations:Post Office:
  Dress up like a mail carrier\, sort mail\, and deliver letters and packag
 es just like a real mail carrier!Veterinary Office: Care for stuffed anima
 l patients as a vet\, complete with checkups and bandages.Diner: Serve up 
 delicious imaginary meals as a chef or take orders as a friendly server.Wi
 th plenty of props\, costumes\, and open-ended activities\, your child can
  explore new roles\, practice social skills\, and have a blast.  No regist
 ration is required—just drop in and play!Each family group must include 
 a responsible adult in the room at all times. This program is for children
  2 to 7 years old only! While other ages are welcome in the room\, we kind
 ly ask that the play area and toys remain reserved exclusively for the int
 ended age group to ensure a safe environment for young participants.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Lapp Story Silo
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/dramatic-play-friday-169
 343
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/american-disasters-166365"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:American Disasters
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T140000
UID:2754dc95a699ec557c401d6d2356fd09@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Discussion\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nBest for adult
 s and older interested teens. Registration is appreciated but not required
  if space allows.American Disasters is a six-session PowerPoint series. Dr
 . Robert Frick\, historian and presenter\, will share the stories and fact
 s related to six events that significantly impacted the United States. The
  stories of the Great Chicago Fire of 1871\, the Johnstown Flood of 1889\,
  the San Francisco Earthquake of 1906\, Hurricane Agnes in the Susquehanna
  Basin in 1972\, the Asian Flu Pandemic of 1957-58\, and the Sinking of th
 e USS Indianapolis will be shared during this program. Participants should
  prepare for lively presentations filled with interesting facts and pepper
 ed with humor. Dr. Frick’s goal is education with a smile.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/american-disasters-16636
 5
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
