BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/all-about-owls-198206"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:All About Owls
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T170000
UID:8a653749ee153cef6e137721586eaa77@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Children\n\nLearn about owls and th
 e role they play in the ecosystem by dissecting real owl pellets with a La
 ncaster County Parks Naturalist.Owls swallow their prey whole\, so they ev
 entually have to spit what they can’t digest back up\, packed into a tig
 ht bundle – an owl pellet. Owl pellets are valuable to scientists becaus
 e they provide information about an owl’s diet and the types of prey ava
 ilable in its habitat. For this hands-on learning experience\, participant
 s will examine and identify the contents of their owl pellet – bones\, f
 ur\, feathers\, etc.Ages 5-10Space is limited | Registration is required
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Program Room A + B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/all-about-owls-198206
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
