 o programs each week\, differentiated by child’s age. If you have childr
 en in both groups\, you may participate in both or choose a different one 
 each week to get the maximum benefit! Please register for all dates you pl
 an to attend!10 am-11 am –  Parent-child workshop (birth to 3 with careg
 iver) -providing a welcoming community environment with resources that fam
 ilies need to nurture their children’s development to help ensure they e
 nter school ready and able to learn.Weekly topics:October 7: Early Literac
 y with Quarryville Library Youth staff plus FREE vision care screenings co
 urtesy of Vision CorpsOctober 14: Speech and Language Development with Lan
 caster County Intervention October 21: Growth and Development with Thrive 
 to Five / Parents as TeachersOctober 28: Pediatric Nutrition with Penn Sta
 te ExtensionNovember 4: Music and Movement plus "Touch-a-Truck" ambulance 
 and Family Safety with Wakefield EMSEach week offers opportunities for chi
 ldren to play with developmentally appropriate toys in a play group settin
 g and for parents to meet and question community experts in the areas of c
 hild development\, speech and language\, nutrition\, play\, movement\, and
  music.Learn more about what it means to be a Family Place library on our 
 website!
