X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-historical-society-event-161153"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Mills of Lancaster County: An Afternoon with Historian Donald Kaut
 z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T160000
UID:155a6d32b3b9f0759ad721823ce896af@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nStep back in ti
 me with author Donald Kautz and the Manheim Township Historical Society as
  we explore the history of Lancaster County’s water-powered grist mills.
  From the ingenious engineering of the waterwheel to the personal stories 
 of the families who kept them running\, this presentation brings our local
  heritage to life. Join us to discover the secret history of these iconic 
 structures and see how they continue to shape our landscape today.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center AB
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-historical-soci
 ety-event-161153
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
